    - target: {fileID: 6822533329394676782, guid: 865a393ffc72f674081048c5d8441f4e, type: 3}
      propertyPath: m_text
      value: "Incompressible \uFB02uids have to speed up when they reach a narrow-cross
        section area in order to maintain a constant volume \uFB02ow rate. So, at
        constant flow rate the value for calculating the theoretical velocity is
        found as:  V<size=65%>th</size> = Q \xF7 A\n\nSuch that:\nQ is a flow rate
        in (m^3/s)\nA is a cross-section area in (m^2)\n\nBut in venturi tube, only
        a little amount of the total pressure head that measured by the pitot tube
        will be converted to a dynamic head. So, the velocity can be measured using
        the equation:\n\nVexp = \u221A(2ghdyn)\n\n\n"
      objectReference: {fileID: 0}
